-- title:
--   Inertia-field valuation ring: a DVR with uniformiser p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $p$, meaning that the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from the subring $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$ into $A$, and assume that composing $\rho$ with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ gives the structure map $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Write $F$ for the fixed field of the image in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $O$ for the pullback of $A$ along $F \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. The assertion is that there exist ring homomorphisms $\iota : O \to A$ and $\rho_O : \mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to O$ such that: the image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\iota(o)$ is the image of $o$ under $F \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for every $o \in O$; $\iota \circ \rho_O = \rho$; $\iota$ is injective; $O$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$; $\iota(o)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ exactly when $o$ lies in that of $O$; the map $o \mapsto \mathrm{residue}_A(\iota(o))$ onto the residue field of $A$ is surjective; and every element $\tau$ of the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ that lies in the inertia subgroup satisfies $\tau \cdot \iota(o) = \iota(o)$ for all $o \in O$.
--
--   This packages the unramifiedness of $A$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ along the inertia field: the valuation ring of the inertia subfield is a discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $p$ and with the same residue field as $A$, together with the inclusion into $A$ and a compatible structure map. It is used as the coefficient-ring input for base change of charts on models of modular curves at $p$, for instance by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart_valuationSubring`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart_valuationSubring) and the neighbouring crossing-chart results.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_exists_ringHom_comap_fixedField_inertiaSubgroupIn_comp_eq_and_isDiscreteValuationRing.lean

